# T9AMAIL

Web email client for a HMD feature phone (Opera Mini Extreme, 2.4"
screen). Part of T9A, a set of small apps for the phone; sibling apps
live in their own repos (T9A-map, T9A-drive).

Pages are plain HTML. Mail is read from a local copy, so the web app
never makes IMAP calls.

## What it does
- Inbox (/list): newest first. "(N)" marks messages not yet opened on
  the phone. Links at the top: switcher, compose, refresh.
- Tap a message to see the body with From, Subject and Date (/view),
  with [reply], [list] and a Hide button.
- Reply: threaded reply to the sender.
- Compose: new message to an address chosen from a contacts list
  (~/.t9a_contacts, one `name address` per line). Only listed
  addresses are accepted.
- Read and hidden state are kept on the phone side only (seen.txt,
  hidden.txt). Posteo is never changed. Both files are discarded if
  the mailbox UIDVALIDITY changes, so a mailbox reset can't hide
  new mail.

## How it works
- mbsync (cron, every minute via sync_cron.sh, with a lock file to
  prevent overlap) pulls the Posteo INBOX into ~/Mail/INBOX. The sync
  is pull-only. MaxMessages in ~/.mbsyncrc keeps the local copy small
  on purpose: the app is for short, conversational messages, not an
  archive.
- pager.sh writes headers.txt (UID, read status, From, Subject, Date,
  warning flag from classify_mail.py).
- app.py (Bottle, port 80) lists, views, replies and composes.
  Sender-controlled text is escaped, and uids must be numeric.
- Messages are sent by send_json.sh, which POSTs to the Resend API.
  From is hello@omegasemantic.org, which forwards to the Posteo
  inbox. HTTPS is used because the VPS host blocks SMTP.
- Only one of the T9A apps holds port 80 at a time. /switch/<name>
  runs /root/restart, which stops the others and starts the one chosen.

## Deploy
Edit and commit on the dev machine, then push. On the server:

    git pull
    ./venv/bin/python -m py_compile app.py && echo OK
    /root/restart mail

Only restart if OK printed. To switch back to another app:
`/root/restart <app>`.

## To rebuild on a new machine
- Python venv with bottle: `python3 -m venv venv && venv/bin/pip install bottle`
- ~/.resendrc containing RESEND_API_KEY=...  (never commit)
- ~/.mbsyncrc for the Posteo account, plus the Maildir ~/Mail/INBOX
- ~/.t9a_contacts for the compose dropdown
- cron: `* * * * * <path>/sync_cron.sh`
- systemd unit t9amail-web.service (runs `venv/bin/python app.py`)
- /root/restart, the script behind the switcher
- Timezone for terminal-tool dates defaults to Pacific/Auckland
  (mail_helpers.sh)

## Runtime files (gitignored, server only)
headers.txt, mail.raw, request.json, sync_cron.log, seen.txt, hidden.txt

## Files
app.py, send_json.sh, static/ (web app); pager.sh, classify_mail.py,
sync_cron.sh, mail_helpers.sh (sync pipeline); browser.sh, tmail.sh,
reply.sh (older terminal client); webproto/ (superseded prototype);
CLAUDE.md, TODO (working notes).
